\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ye neighbours and friends of 
\par Jesus draw near:
\par His love condescends by titles so dear
\par To call and invite you 
\par His triumph to prove,
\par And freely delight you in Jesus's love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The Shepherd who died  
\par His sheep to redeem;
\par On every side are gathered to Him
\par The weary and burdened, the reprobate race;
\par And wait to be pardoned through
\par Jesus's grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The blind are restored through 
\par Jesus's name,
\par They see their dear Lord, and 
\par follow the Lamb;
\par The halt they are walking,
\par and running their tace,
\par The dumb they are talking of 
\par Jesus's grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The deah hear His voice and 
\par comforting Word,
\par It bids them rejoice in Jesus their Lord:
\par Thy sins are forgiven, accepted thou art;
\par They listen, and heaven springs up 
\par in the heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. The lepers from all their spots are 
\par made clean,
\par The dead by His call are raised
\par from their sin;
\par In Jesu's compassion the sick find
\par a cure,
\par And gospel salvation is preached
\par to the poor.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. They seek Him and find: they ask
\par and recieve
\par The Friend of mankind, who 
\par bids thembelieve:
\par On Jesus they venture, His gift they embrace,
\par And forcibly enter His kingdom of grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O Jesus, ride on till all are subdued,
\par Thy mercy make known, and sprinkle
\par Thy blood;
\par Display Thy salvation, and teach
\par the new song
\par To every nation, and people, and tongue.
\par                                             Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
